{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Dimension and Measurement Unit.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Dimension and Measurement Unit.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"physical dimension and measurement unit physical dimension and measurement unit","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Dimension and Measurement Unit.md","fileName":"Physical Dimension and Measurement Unit.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Physical Dimension and Measurement Unit","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Unit Algebra and Measurement Precision]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Unit Algebra and Measurement Precision","Dimensional Homogeneity in Equations","Seven SI Base Units","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Dimension and Measurement Unit.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Dimension and Measurement Unit.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"physical dimension and measurement unit physical dimension and measurement unit","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Dimension and Measurement Unit.md","fileName":"Physical Dimension and Measurement Unit.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Physical Dimension and Measurement Unit","heading":"Physical Dimension and Measurement Unit","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A physical dimension identifies the kind of measurable quantity, while a unit names a scale used to state its value. The book's base-unit table pairs length with meter, time with second, and mass with kilogram. A length can therefore be recorded in different units without becoming a different kind of quantity. Derived quantities combine dimensions algebraically, which is why their unit expressions can be checked by [[Dimensional Homogeneity in